    "blocks": [
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "thm",
        "label": {
          "en": "▲ Parametric & polar",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "For a parametric curve, \\( \\dfrac{dy}{dx}=\\dfrac{dy/dt}{dx/dt} \\). Polar area is \\( \\displaystyle A=\\tfrac12\\int_\\alpha^\\beta r^2\\,d\\theta. \\)",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "thm",
        "label": {
          "en": "▲ Series convergence",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "The ratio test: \\( \\sum a_n \\) converges absolutely if \\( \\displaystyle\\lim_{n\\to\\infty}\\Big|\\dfrac{a_{n+1}}{a_n}\\Big|<1 \\). Taylor series and their intervals of convergence are the centrepiece of Unit 10.",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "thm",
        "label": {
          "en": "▲ BC-only topics",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "AP Calculus BC extends AB with additional integration techniques, convergence tests, parametric/polar calculus, and infinite series — approximately 40% of the exam is BC-exclusive material.",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "cards",
        "items": [
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "BC-only: Series",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "Taylor/Maclaurin, ratio test, alternating series, error bounds",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "BC-only: Parametric",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "Slope \\( \\frac{dy/dt}{dx/dt} \\), arc length, speed \\( =\\sqrt{(x')^2+(y')^2} \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "BC-only: Polar",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "Area \\( \\frac{1}{2}\\int r^2\\,d\\theta \\), arc length, slope in polar",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "BC-only: Techniques",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "Integration by parts, partial fractions, improper integrals, Euler's method",
              "ar": null
            }
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
